Grafana logs an ERROR on every boot when this directory does not exist:

  Failed to read plugin provisioning files from directory
  path=/etc/grafana/provisioning/plugins error="no such file or directory"

Harmless -- no plugin is provisioned this way; GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS in
docker-compose.yml is what installs the ECharts panel -- but it is logged at
error level, so it lands in the NAS Container Logs "Errors and warnings" panel
twice per restart and crowds the one view that has to stay readable.

An empty directory is enough to silence it. Git cannot track one, hence this
file. Grafana only reads *.yaml/*.yml here, so this text is ignored.
